Relevant columns and how they will be used  
(reference_name = “chr1” AND start_position BETWEEN 55 039 447 AND 55 064 852)

• reference_name : to restrict the search to chromosome 1  
• start_position : left‐hand bound of the region  
• end_position : right‐hand bound of each variant (not strictly required but useful for inspection)  
• alternate_bases.alt : the actual alternate allele(s) present at the locus  
• alternate_bases.AC : allele count (per alternate allele) – add to obtain “total allele count”  
• AN : total number of called alleles at the locus – add to obtain “total number of alleles”  
• alternate_bases.vep.SYMBOL : gene symbol(s) assigned by the Variant Effect Predictor – collect distinct values  

Typical filter condition  
reference_name = 'chr1' AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852  


10 exploratory → final BigQuery SQL statements  
(only the table bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1 is touched; every query ends with LIMIT 20)

```sql
