Relevant columns and how they will be used  
(reference_name = “chr1” AND start_position BETWEEN 55 039 447 AND 55 064 852)

• reference_name : to restrict the search to chromosome 1  
• start_position : left‐hand bound of the region  
• end_position : right‐hand bound of each variant (not strictly required but useful for inspection)  
• alternate_bases.alt : the actual alternate allele(s) present at the locus  
• alternate_bases.AC : allele count (per alternate allele) – add to obtain “total allele count”  
• AN : total number of called alleles at the locus – add to obtain “total number of alleles”  
• alternate_bases.vep.SYMBOL : gene symbol(s) assigned by the Variant Effect Predictor – collect distinct values  

Typical filter condition  
reference_name = 'chr1' AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852  


10 exploratory → final BigQuery SQL statements  
(only the table bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1 is touched; every query ends with LIMIT 20)

```sql
-- 1. Peek at raw variant rows in the interval
SELECT
  reference_name,
  start_position,
  end_position,
  reference_bases,
  alternate_bases
FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1`
WHERE reference_name = 'chr1'
  AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Show distinct alternate allele strings found in the region
SELECT DISTINCT
  alt.alt AS alternate_allele
FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1`,
     UNNEST(alternate_bases) AS alt
WHERE reference_name = 'chr1'
  AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Inspect allele counts (AC) for every alternate allele
SELECT
  start_position,
  alt.alt,
  alt.AC AS allele_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1`,
     UNNEST(alternate_bases) AS alt
WHERE reference_name = 'chr1'
  AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852
ORDER BY start_position
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Distinct gene symbols (VE*P) reported in this segment
SELECT DISTINCT
  vep_entry.SYMBOL AS gene_symbol
FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1`,
     UNNEST(alternate_bases) AS alt,
     UNNEST(alt.vep)        AS vep_entry
WHERE reference_name = 'chr1'
  AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852
  AND vep_entry.SYMBOL IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Summed allele count (AC) per variant row
SELECT
  start_position,
  SUM(alt.AC) AS total_AC_per_variant
FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1`,
     UNNEST(alternate_bases) AS alt
WHERE reference_name = 'chr1'
  AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852
GROUP BY start_position
ORDER BY start_position
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Summed AN (total alleles) per variant row
SELECT
  start_position,
  AN AS total_called_alleles
FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1`
WHERE reference_name = 'chr1'
  AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852
ORDER BY start_position
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Variant count only (one record per row in the table)
SELECT
  COUNT(*) AS variant_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1`
WHERE reference_name = 'chr1'
  AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Variant density: region length divided by #variants (simple preview)
WITH region AS (
  SELECT 55064852 - 55039447 AS region_length
),
var_count AS (
  SELECT COUNT(*) AS n_var
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1`
  WHERE reference_name = 'chr1'
    AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852
)
SELECT
  region_length / n_var AS region_length_per_variant
FROM region, var_count
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Position, gene symbol(s), allele count – one row per alt allele
SELECT
  t.start_position,
  vep_entry.SYMBOL AS gene_symbol,
  alt.AC           AS allele_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1` AS t
JOIN UNNEST(t.alternate_bases) AS alt
JOIN UNNEST(alt.vep)           AS vep_entry
ON TRUE
WHERE t.reference_name = 'chr1'
  AND t.start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852
ORDER BY t.start_position
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final one‑row summary: #variants, total AC, total AN, distinct gene list, density
WITH base AS (
  SELECT
    start_position,
    SUM(alt.AC) AS sum_AC_per_variant,
    ANY_VALUE(AN) AS AN_per_variant,
    ARRAY_AGG(DISTINCT vep_entry.SYMBOL IGNORE NULLS) AS symbols
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1`,
       UNNEST(alternate_bases) AS alt
  LEFT JOIN UNNEST(alt.vep) AS vep_entry
  ON TRUE
  WHERE reference_name = 'chr1'
    AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852
  GROUP BY start_position
)
SELECT
  COUNT(*)                                        AS variant_count,
  SUM(sum_AC_per_variant)                         AS total_allele_count,
  SUM(AN_per_variant)                             AS total_number_of_alleles,
  ARRAY_TO_STRING(ARRAY(SELECT DISTINCT s FROM UNNEST(symbols) AS s), ', ') AS distinct_gene_symbols,
  (55064852 - 55039447) / COUNT(*)               AS region_length_per_variant
FROM base
LIMIT 20;
```

